<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/065L">Example <span data-tag="065L">9.3.4.3</span> <span class="named">(Flat Modules as Flat Functors)</span>.</a> Let $R$ be an associative ring and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be the category of free left $R$-modules of finite rank. Then a functor $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{Set}$ is flat if and only if it has the form $\operatorname{Hom}_{R}( \bullet , M)$, where $M$ is a flat left $R$-module. This is a reformulation of Lazard's characterization of flat modules (Variant <a data-tag="0659" href="/tag/0659">9.3.2.13</a>), by virtue of Remark <a data-tag="065P" href="/tag/065P">9.3.4.6</a> below. </p>
</article>
